urned (gen.go's"] [103 1 "// resume; queue 210): its object no longer holds it."] [111 1 "// freeFrame clears f into its code's free list (queue 305: the frame zeroed, then its three kept fields put back,"] [112 1 "// half the cost of assigning the literal of the three; the value stack cleared up to its depth only, its slots above"] [113 1 "// SP being nil already: every pop, drop and truncation of the stack clears what it leaves)."] [124 1 "// FrameType is the frame objects' type (sys._getframe, a traceback's tb_frame)."] [129 1 "// Line is the frame's current line (f_lineno), 0 when the code has no lines."] [132 1 "// ReportedLasti is f_lasti: Lasti, or after a reraise N there the instruction it re-raises from."] [157 1 "// popN pops n items and returns them in stack order (a view, valid until the next push)."] [166 1 "// Thread is a Python thread's state (PyThreadState): its current frame, the exception being"] [167 1 "// handled (sys.exception()), the call depth against the recursion limit. One thread runs at a time"] [168 1 "// (the GIL: PYS10 (a), PY6)."] [172 17 "// the exception being handled at this level (None outside handlers): the frame's or generator's slot"] [173 2 "// outer are the slots of the levels a running generator or coroutine was resumed from (CPython's exc_info"] [174 2 "// stack, gi_exc_state's previous_item): sys.exception() is the first that is not None (CurrentHandled)"] [177 2 "// cdepth is the C level's depth (PY7): the nested built-in calls CPython guards by _Py_EnterRecursiveCall"] [178 2 "// (comparison, repr, str, a tuple's hash, isinstance's and issubclass's recursions, the eval loop entered from"] [179 2 "// C), which CPython 3.14 measures on the machine's stack and pyi counts (enterRecursiveCall)"] [181 2 "// direct is the number of direct calls (callDirect: a compiled caller's Go frames under its compiled callee's"] [182 2 "// loop) nested on the thread's Go stack, at most directMax (queue 216d)"] [184 26 "// the containers being repr'd (Py_ReprEnter)"] [185 26 "// callStack's signal, reused (202b)"] [186 2 "// asyncio_running_loop and asyncio_running_task of the thread state (_asyncio, queue 224), nil when none"] [188 30 "// the current context (context.c: the thread state's), nil until first asked"] [189 2 "// finPend are the objects with a __del__ this thread's frames made, not yet checked at a frame's return, and"] [190 2 "// finPendDepth the deepest of their frames' depths, 0 when none (finalize.go's finAtReturn: the moment at a frame's"] [191 2 "// return, the user's decision of 2026-11-22)"] [196 1 "// CurrentHandled is the exception being handled (_PyErr_GetTopmostException): this level's slot, else the"] [197 1 "// first not None of the levels it was resumed from; None when none is."] [210 1 "// chainContext is _PyErr_SetObject's implicit chaining: exc's __context__ the exception being handled, a cycle"] [211 1 "// through exc in that chain cut first."] [229 10 "// a cycle not through exc"] [239 1 "// reprEnter is Py_ReprEnter: true when o is already being repr'd (a recursive container: \"[...]\")."] [251 1 "// reprLeave is Py_ReprLeave."] [254 1 "// The C level's stack (PY7). CPython 3.14 raises RecursionError \"Stack overflow (used N kB)WHERE\" when a guarded"] [255 1 "// built-in call (_Py_EnterRecursiveCall) finds the machine's stack past its soft limit; a Python frame does not use it."] [256 1 "// pyi's built-ins recurse on Go's stack, a goroutine's at most 1 GB, which a deep enough structure overflowed (a fatal"] [257 1 "// Go error: test_tuple's test_hash_deeply_nested, test_copy's reflexive comparisons, test_isinstance's recursions)."] [258 1 "// pyi counts the guarded levels instead, and Go's calls into the machine (Thread.run: the eval loop entered from C,"] [259 1 "// where \"\"): cStackLevels of them, cFrameBytes each as the message's nominal kB (about"] [260 1 "// CPython's 1 MB soft limit on Linux); CPython's own depth varies with the call (on Alpine aarch64 a tuple's hash"] [261 1 "// reaches 10,000 levels, its repr not)."] [267 1 "// enterRecursiveCall is _Py_EnterRecursiveCall(where): false, with the RecursionError, past the limit; else the"] [268 1 "// level is entered and leaveRecursiveCall leaves it."] [281 1 "// stackOverflow is _Py_CheckRecursiveCall's RecursionError."] [286 1 "// leaveRecursiveCall is _Py_LeaveRecursiveCall for enterRecursiveCall's thread."] [295 1 "// currentThread is the running thread (the GIL's holder)."] [298 1 "// unbound is the marker :load-fast-and-clear pushes for an unbound local (PEP 709)."] [305 1 "// newFrame makes the frame of a function's call with its arguments bound (CPython's"] [306 1 "// _PyEval_MakeFrameVector); args holds the positional then the keyword arguments."] [317 3 "// the fast locals and the value stack in one allocation (202b): the stack's room the most the code's"] [318 3 "// frames have needed (Code.stackHint, kept by runFrames at a return), so a call does not grow it from nothing"] [324 3 "// a module's or a class body's code called as a function (types.FunctionType(code, globals): the asyncio REPL's"] [325 3 "// statements, queue 293): its names are the globals, as _PyFunction_Vectorcall gives _PyEval_Vector the"] [326 3 "// function's globals as the frame's locals for a code without CO_OPTIMIZED"] [337 13 "// _tracemalloc's allocation (queue 220): the caller's, the callee not entered yet"] [352 1 "// bindArgs puts a call's arguments into the parameters' slots (positional, *args, keyword-only,"] [353 1 "// **kwargs, then the defaults), raising CPython's TypeErrors (Python/ceval.c's, with the qualified name)."] [357 20 "// every parameter given by position (queue 210: the common call, without the general path)"] [472 1 "// joinNames is CPython's list of names: 'a', 'a' and 'b', 'a', 'b', and 'c'."] [497 1 "// newGeneratorHook makes the generator, coroutine or async generator object of a call's frame (its"] [498 1 "// code flagged :generator or :coroutine): PY5d's gen.g